# Marker-selected region recombination

Design: parse four equal rectangular panels separated by a uniform frame. The
first panel contains an eight-connected dividing path and an isolated singleton
of the same color. Remove the singleton and flood the four-connected open region
containing its coordinate. Copy source panel two into that marked region and panel three into the other
region. On the dividing path overlay both sources transparently, with panel two
winning nonbackground conflicts. Write only panel four.
The alternative swaps the two source roles, with identical inputs.

Implementation checklist: literal and all original-label regressions; independent
Racket boundary detection and flood; standalone generator and matched adapter;
2..6 demos / 1..4 prefix-stable queries; finite topology/marker/overlay rivals;
strict masked shuffled presentation; protected original/preflight/causal labels;
source-bound copied-runtime and relocation checks. No original data/authority edits.

30x30 remains four horizontal panels, not a reinterpretation of panel order:
28x6 content, one extra frame column and ordinary top/bottom frames. Payloads and
selector occupy the full height; frame thickness is discovered rather than fixed.

Original train[1] exposed a real boundary case: source-two background cannot
erase source-three ink on the divider. The general transparent-overlay rule
replaces the initially exclusive boundary assignment; its literal regression
is retained. The original data and labels are unchanged.

Adversarial self-review repaired three specific lesson holes. Straight-line-only
minimum lessons allowed eight-neighbor flooding; a shallow jog also permitted
bounding-box selection. The first demo now has a deeper nonrectangular jog with
an explicit wrong-bounding-box disagreement. The second selects the opposite,
larger open region. Every generated scene exhibits both one-source-transparent
boundary cases and an overlapping-ink priority case. These constraints hold for
both settings, without changing their matched inputs. All eighteen declared
rivals are eliminated by the minimum two demos in the retained finite audit.

Current result: all five original labels, 43 copied-runtime tests, a 32-seed /
320-lesson audit and 91 additional protected-reference cases pass. The wrong-ink
mask counterfactual changes 101 cells; six generator-only relocated labels and
sixteen masked public views pass. Grammar: four equal rectangular horizontal
panels, one uniform frame color excluded from panel content, an initially blank
fourth panel, one divider and one isolated singleton, exactly two four-connected
open regions. These are authoring checks, not owner approval or training admission.
